From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: drm: dw-hdmi: support allwinner,force-connected DT property

Some embedded HDMI panels (including internal bridge boards) expose no
usable HPD signal and no reliable EDID path. In that setup, the generic
DW-HDMI detect path can keep reporting disconnected and block modeset.

Allow boards to opt in to forced connector status via a DT boolean on the
DW-HDMI controller node:

  allwinner,force-connected;

When present, detect always returns connector_status_connected.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2447,6 +2447,13 @@ static void dw_hdmi_update_phy_mask(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi)
 static enum drm_connector_status dw_hdmi_detect(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi)
 {
 	enum drm_connector_status result;
+
+	/*
+	 * Boards with internal HDMI bridges may not expose HPD/EDID. Allow a
+	 * DT opt-in override to force connector presence and unblock modeset.
+	 */
+	if (hdmi->dev->of_node && of_property_read_bool(hdmi->dev->of_node, "allwinner,force-connected"))
+		return connector_status_connected;
 
 	result = hdmi->phy.ops->read_hpd(hdmi, hdmi->phy.data);
 	hdmi->last_connector_result = result;
-- 
